		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3198&amp;p=28269#p28269"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div></div></blockquote>Well, i have modified lines in the pi-star to work (at least) rd5r (with opengd77) in ipsc2/dmr+.<br>....................................................................................................................................<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2055&amp;sid=6e279bbcc5ac575a5fa0bfe30ea9eb0c" class="postimage" alt="dmrgw1.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div> Here de initial configuration, mod working only in DMRGateway.<br>.....................................................................................................................................<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2056&amp;sid=6e279bbcc5ac575a5fa0bfe30ea9eb0c" class="postimage" alt="dmrgw2.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div> Here the copy/paste overwrited lines from ipsc2 over Brandmeister  <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_mrgreen.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":mrgreen:" title="Mr. Green"><br>.....................................................................................................................................<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2057&amp;sid=6e279bbcc5ac575a5fa0bfe30ea9eb0c" class="postimage" alt="dmrgw3.png" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div> Set Brandmeister active (in DMRGateway) BEFORE any mod! After mod do not apply changes al all in the graphical "Configurations" menu!!!<br>Just only (press apply in editor) in "Expert" and "DMR GW", then you can safetly reboot but no need. If you reboot will need a longer time to get the DMR button from red to green but it will. In "Configuration" menu you will loose modded settings if apply changes!<br>And you can restore Brandmeister settings (the original one) if you choose the DMR/Brandmeister Master and your country (apply changes) and get rid (or put "#" before line) for "Options="StartRef=..." line. Or write the original lines in editor (Expert/DMD GW) manually down.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=896">YO3VTH</a> — Tue Dec 26, 2023 7:29 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
