		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3198&amp;p=28236#p28236"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>TS1_2=2; TS2_3=2263</div></blockquote>Does not look correct, but I don't know whether that would cause problems<br><br>Normally the default TS are defined as<br><br>TS1_1=2;<br>TS2_1=2263;<br><br>i.e. the nomenclature for this is<br><br>TSx i.e the TS number TS1 or TS2<br><br>Followed by a number which indicates the index which starts with 1<br><br>See <br><br><a href="https://vkdmr.com/connect-your-hotspot/" class="postlink">https://vkdmr.com/connect-your-hotspot/</a><br><br>You can define multiple TGs per TS e.g<br><br>TS1_1=5;TS1_2=3801;TS1_3=3802;<br><br>This tells IPSC to create static routes for inbound traffic on TG5, TG3801 and TG3802 for TS1<br><br><br>I recommdend you check your codeplug and also your hotspot configuation, becuase the values you are currently using are defintely sub optimal and may not even work.<br><br>BTW.<br><br>Make sure you have not enabled TA Tx for the channel, as DMR MARC / DMR+ / IPSC2 does not support in-call data and it causes problems if you enable it, even though Talker Alias is defined in the ETSI DMR specification.<br>The problem is that IPSC (Motorola) is a proprietary and partially not fully ETSI standard compliant.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Dec 23, 2023 11:43 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
