<blockquote class="uncited"><div>"Looks much more to be a network/configuration issue" </div></blockquote>There are more strange things in Bucharest, here on ipsc2. <br>I tried through hotspot even direct connection to our local repeaters. <a href="https://yodmr.blogspot.com/2019/04/yo3d-si-yo3e-update.html" class="postlink">https://yodmr.blogspot.com/2019/04/yo3d ... pdate.html</a><br>The same. RX ok and no TX. <br><br>Well, our ipsc2/dmr+... has a bridged connection to the repeater(s), the repeaters are using SmartPTT software/hardware, based on Motorola.<br>In the last hour a few people tried Private Calls (or data transfer, aprs and so on) and i think the lines was overworked (call over another call).<br>I think the guys (that used Private Calls) should buy GSM mobile phones and talk in them (for private calls). <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><br>If you think my radio values in the radio (the pictures attached earlier) is fine, then my radio is fine too.<div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2049&amp;sid=6e279bbcc5ac575a5fa0bfe30ea9eb0c" class="postimage" alt="highlander.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div>And yes, i have two DMR radios. The RD5R with openGD77 and another expensive Motorola-based radio.<br>The expensive one are working fine RX/TX.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=896">YO3VTH</a> — Sat Dec 23, 2023 3:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
