<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Greetings! <br><br>Can i ask for an original RD-5R flash backup (my radio is from radioddity, i'm the first user) please?<br>Now i have upgraded to 2023.12.12 - all fine in Brandmeister (RX/TX) but - i have RX in ipsc2 and no TX there, only a "click-sound".<br><br>And how to calibrate the RD-5R? I see the screen 1/4 - how can i move forward to 2/4 3/4 and 4/4?<br>I would like to calibrate in 145 and not in 135mhz.<br><br>I think i messed up somehow the original values and i have no backups made <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"><br><br>Thanks!<br><br>That's my actual values: uhf1.pngvhf1.png<br>Maibe should reverse here something?: band.png</div></blockquote>If it works fine on Brandmeister but not on IPSC2 (DMR MARC / DMR+) then the problem is not your calibration, but is in your codeplug.<br><br>Why do you think the calibration is wrong? <br><br>Did you change some values at random ?<br><br><br>Restoring someone else's RD5R flash backup into your radio will cause problems with the calibration, becuase the calibration is specific to each radio.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Dec 23, 2023 2:37 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
